<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU cuts 1997/98 flax area aid payments.</title>
<headline>EU cuts 1997/98 flax area aid payments.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers agreed on Wednesday to cut flax area aid payments by 5.7 percent to 815.86 ecus per hectare, the EU said in a statement.</p>
<p>The hemp area aid was reduced by 7.5 percent to 716.63 ecus per hectare.</p>
<p>A flax market promotion levy of 49.62 ecus a tonne was reduced to zero but aid payments to producers were left unchanged.</p>
<p>The changes were part of a set of farm prices agreed after a three-day Farm Council meeting in Luxembourg.</p>
</text>
